# 🎯 Expectations - Notebook LLM Project

## 1. Development Principles

- Use **modular code structure** and scalable architecture
- Maintain **100% traceability** from raw data to generated response
- Enforce **AI grounding rules** (no hallucinations, always reference source)
- Promote **team clarity** via shared docs, tickets, and design specs
- Maintain high **collaboration frequency** via weekly demos

---

## 2. Engineering Expectations

| Area | Expectation |
|------|-------------|
| ✅ Code Quality | PEP8-compliant, tested, typed (where possible) |
| 🧪 Test Coverage | > 80% coverage for core modules |
| 🔐 Security | JWT auth, file sanitization, safe prompt injection |
| 📄 Documentation | Every module must be self-documented |
| ⛓️ Dependency Control | Lock file (`requirements.lock.txt`) tracked in repo |
| ⏱️ Performance | Queries under 3 seconds for small docs (<5MB) |
| 📊 Monitoring | Basic logs + query tracking |

---

## 3. Design Expectations

- Consistent component naming
- Responsive UI
- A11y compliant (screen reader, keyboard nav)
- Clear UX flows with breadcrumbs and context

---

## 4. AI Output Expectations

| Rule | Description |
|------|-------------|
| ✅ Confidence Flag | Output should include confidence score |
| ✅ Source Linking | Answers must cite retrieved chunk |
| ❌ No Guessing | Do not guess if document lacks answer |
| ✅ Decomposition | Complex queries should be split logically |
